Rules:
  [G1] Always profile before optimizing â€” use `go test -bench` and `pprof`.
  [G2] Minimize allocations in hot paths â€” reuse objects with sync.Pool.
  [G3] Use `[]byte` buffers instead of string concatenation.
  [G4] Pre-allocate slices when size is known.
  [G5] Use `strconv` instead of `fmt.Sprintf` for numbers.
  [G6] Avoid mutex contention â€” use sharding or atomic operations.
  [G7] Use `runtime.SetFinalizer` carefully for cleanup.
  [G8] Monitor GC pauses with `GOGC` and `GOMEMLIMIT`.
  [G9] Use `go tool trace` for CPU and goroutine analysis.
  [G10] Benchmark with realistic data, not synthetic tests.

